<title>PORTUGAL: Price rises slightly on Portugal variable bonds.</title>
<headline>Price rises slightly on Portugal variable bonds.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average price rose to 99.5293 at the Portuguese Institute of Public Credit Management's auction of seven-year bonds from 99.3457 previously.</p>
<p>ISSUER: Republic of Portugal   AMOUNT PLACED:14.7 billion</p>
<p>INTEREST: Six-month Lisbor less 25 basis points</p>
<p>MATURITY: 30/7/04   PAYMENT DATE: 22/4/97</p>
<p>COUPON PAYMENT: Six-monthly</p>
<p>AVERAGE PRICE:99.5293 MAX PRICE:99.64 MINIMUM:99.50</p>
<p>BIDS:56.55 billion escudos TOTAL ISSUED:67.6</p>
<p>Note - The issue is fungible.</p>
</text>
